  "description": "BEPKIR crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group P 42/n n m. Reported CIF formula moiety: C180 H224 Nd8 O72 S16,4(C1 H4 O1),28(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd2E (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd1K (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd2J (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd1I (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd2O (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd1D (Nd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 8 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 4.071-4.071 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 106.70-110.59°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C184H296Nd8O104S16. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 8 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
